after 82 days underground these wounded  ukrainian soldiers are finally leaving  the azov style steel plant on russian  buses displaying the letter zed symbolic  of its invasion  for months these fighters from the azov  battalion attempted to defend the steel  plant in mariopol and prevent russian  soldiers from completely taking over the  port city but outnumbered and  overpowered ukraine says its mission to  defend the plant is  the over of mario paul fulfilled all the  tasks set by their commanders  unfortunately we do not have the  opportunity to unblock as of style by  military means  the fight for the steelworks and the  plight of civilians and fighters trapped  there captured the world's attention all  women children and elderly have already  been rescued president vladimir zelinsky  says the priority now is to move out the  rest of the fighters still in the plants  thanks to the actions of the ukrainian  military the international committee of  the red cross and the un we hope that we  will be able to save the lives of our  guys there are severely wounded soldiers  among them they've been given care i  want to stress that ukraine needs  ukrainian heroes alive  those seriously wounded have been taken  to a medical facility in the  russian-controlled town of navo azovsk  they could become part of a prisoner  swap  ukrainian fighters say they held out in  avastar for weeks to buy time for the  rest of ukraine to battle russian forces  and secure western arms needed to  withstand russia's assault  but the evacuation marks the end of what  could be one of the longest and most  bloody battles of the ukraine war  mariopol is now in ruins and ukraine  says tens of thousands of people have  died victoria gatenbee al jazeera  [Applause]
 

